\ Phase 7 slice 5: `tabulate` — allocate an array and fill each slot by
\ splicing an inline quotation that produces a fresh value.  Each slot gets
\ a distinct, freshly-constructed value (never a replicated one), so a linear
\ element type is safe — the synthesized array destructor drops each slot.
\
\ This example uses `i64` (a `Copy` element) for simplicity; the linear-element
\ golden lives in `tests/phase7_slice5_array_drop.rs`.

import: intrinsics * ;
import: core::prelude * ;

\ Build a 5-element array where each slot holds its own index.
: main ( -- )
  5 ~[ 42 ] tabulate | arr |
  &arr 0 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 1 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 2 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 3 >usize &> @ .
  &arr 4 >usize &> @ .
  arr drop ;
